the Heartbeat is a special type of log signal used to indicate that a monitored machine (VM or server) is alive and connected.

Basically, The Heartbeat is a record sent at regular intervals (typically every 1 minute) by the Azure Monitor Agent (or the older Log Analytics Agent) to confirm:

The VM is running

The monitoring agent is installed

The agent is functioning properly

There is network connectivity to Azure Monitor

